  "result": "Excellent! All 130 tests pass (121 existing + 9 new). Here's a summary of the voucher implementation:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Updated: `src/errors.js`**\n- Added `VOUCHER_EXISTS` error code for duplicate voucher attempts\n\n**Updated: `src/invoices.js`**\n\n1. **Modified `invoiceTotals()` function:**\n   - Now returns `voucher` amount (0 if not present)\n   - Updated total calculation: `total = subtotal - discount + vat - voucher`\n   - Total is clamped at 0 (can't go negative)\n\n2. **Added `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` function:**\n   - Applies a fixed-amount voucher to a draft invoice\n   - Sets `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n   - Error handling:\n     - `NOT_DRAFT`: Only works on draft invoices\n     - `VOUCHER_EXISTS`: Prevents applying multiple vouchers\n     - `AMOUNT_INVALID`: Amount must be a positive integer\n   - Does not mutate the input invoice\n\n**Added Tests (9 new tests):**\n- \u2705 invoiceTotals includes zero voucher by default\n- \u2705 applyVoucher adds voucher to draft invoice\n- \u2705 applyVoucher reduces total correctly\n- \u2705 Total is clamped at zero for large vouchers\n- \u2705 Returns NOT_DRAFT for issued invoices\n- \u2705 Returns VOUCHER_EXISTS for duplicate vouchers\n- \u2705 Returns AMOUNT_INVALID for invalid amounts\n- \u2705 Does not mutate input invoice\n- \u2705 invoiceTotals correctly calculates with voucher applied\n\nAll 130 tests pass.",
